Q: @PageableDefault.sort is not overridden even when present in HTTP request A: <p>To fix the issue where the request parameters are ignored, you should separate the pagination defaults from the sorting defaults.
When Spring resolves the Pageable argument, it looks for @SortDefault as a specific instruction for the Sort object. If it finds a sort parameter in the HTTP request, it replaces the entire @SortDefault configuration.</p>
<pre><code>@GetMapping(&quot;/ballotsApi/ballots&quot;)
public Page&lt;BallotDto&gt; getBallots(
    @PageableDefault(size = 20) // probably need
    @SortDefault(sort = &quot;shares&quot;, direction = Sort.Direction.DESC) Pageable page,
    @RequestParam Map&lt;String, String&gt; filters
) {
    log.info(&quot;About to get ballots. Page = {} with filters = {}&quot;, page, filters);

    Page&lt;SearchableBallotProjection&gt; ballots = ballotService.findBallots(page, filters);
    log.info(&quot;Finished Retrieving ballots&quot;);
    return ballots.map(ballotDtoConverter::toDto);
}
</code></pre>

Q: Print variables not found in &quot;unless -e&quot; statement A: <p>This will show you all files that are missing, NOT only first one missing,</p>
<pre><code>@$_ and die &quot;Files missing: @$_\n&quot; 
  for ( grep { !-e } $FileOne, $Filetwo, $FileThree );
</code></pre>

Q: Ng-bootstrap dropdown placement does not work in hostDirective input A: <p>The problem here is that the <code>NgbDropdown</code> directive expects <code>NgbDropdownMenu</code> to be one of its <a href="https://angular.dev/api/core/ContentChildren" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>ContentChildren</code></a>. A content query does not retrieve elements or directives in other components' templates, therfore, the <code>NgbDropdownMenu</code> you have in <code>MyDropdownComponent</code> is not retrieved, which in turn breaks the <code>autoClose</code> logic in <code>NgbDropdown</code>.</p>
<p>Here are two options how you could handle this:</p>
<p><strong>(1)</strong> Make <code>MyDropdownComponent</code> a directive and add the <code>NgbDropdownMenu</code> as content of this directive:</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>  &lt;div myDropdown autoClose=&quot;inside&quot; placement=&quot;bottom&quot;&gt;
    &lt;button myDropdownToggle&gt;
      Options
    &lt;/button&gt;
    &lt;div ngbDropdownMenu&gt;
      &lt;button myDropdownItem&gt;move&lt;/button&gt;
      &lt;button myDropdownItem&gt;rename&lt;/button&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>
<h2><a href="https://stackblitz.com/edit/stackblitz-starters-to5gp7qq?file=src%2Fmain.ts" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Example</a></h2>
<p><strong>(2)</strong> Query <code>NgbDropdownMenu</code> with <code>viewChild</code> and set the internal <code>_menu</code> property (not very clean) of <code>NgbDropdown</code>:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>export class MyDropdownComponent {
  dropdown = inject(NgbDropdown);
  menu = viewChild(NgbDropdownMenu);

  ngAfterViewInit() {
    this.dropdown['_menu'] = this.menu();
  }
}
</code></pre>
<h2><a href="https://stackblitz.com/edit/stackblitz-starters-oo9egdkc?file=src%2Fmain.ts" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Example</a></h2>
